Project Overview

This project performs a basic sales data analysis using Python.
The goal is to analyze sales performance, identify best-selling products, calculate key metrics, and visualize sales trends using charts.

This project demonstrates:

Data loading and cleaning

Sales metric calculations

Basic data visualization

Clear and readable Python code

🎯 Objectives

Calculate total sales and average sales

Identify the best-selling product

Handle missing values safely

Create meaningful visualizations

Generate insights from sales data

🛠️ Technologies Used

Python 3

Pandas – data analysis

Matplotlib – data visualization

📁 Project Structure
sales_project/
│
├── sales_analysis.py      # Main analysis script
├── sales_data.csv         # Sales dataset
├── requirements.txt       # Required Python libraries
└── README.md              # Project documentation

⚙️ Setup Instructions
1️⃣ Install Python Libraries

Run this command in terminal:

pip install pandas matplotlib


Or install using:

pip install -r requirements.txt

2️⃣ Run the Project

Make sure sales_data.csv and sales_analysis.py are in the same folder.

Run:

python sales_analysis.py

📊 Analysis Performed
✅ Data Cleaning

Standardized column names

Filled missing values with zero

Prevented runtime errors using safety checks

✅ Metrics Calculated

Total Sales

Average Sales

Best-Selling Product

✅ Visualizations

Histogram of sales distribution

Bar chart of product-wise sales

📈 Sample Output
Total Sales: 1250000.00
Average Sales: 510.25
Best Selling Product: Laptop


Graphs are displayed automatically using Matplotlib.

🧠 Key Insights

Certain products contribute significantly more revenue

Sales distribution shows purchasing patterns

Data cleaning improves analysis accuracy

🧪 Testing & Validation

Script checks for missing files

Prevents column-related errors

Works with different column name formats
